+### Retained idle-child configuration (registry only)
+
+`globalThis[Symbol.for("pi-subagents:manager")]` also exposes:
+
+- `getIdleChildConfigurationSnapshot(childId)` → `{ status: "ready", childId, snapshot }` or `{ status: "rejected", reason }`.
+- `configureIdleChild({ operationId, childId, expectedSessionId, expectedRevision, model: { provider, id }, thinking, signal? })` → a promise of Pi's `committed`/`noop` receipt (`before`, `after`, `revision`, `operationId`, `notificationErrors`) or `{ status: "rejected", operationId, reason }`.
+- `getIdleChildConfigurationReceipt({ operationId, childId, expectedSessionId })` → an authorized committed receipt or a structured rejection (`not-found` for missing/noop/refused operations).
+
+Only completed retained top-level children of the active root session qualify. Ownership, manager admission generations, context/registry identity, and fresh **mandatory** model scope are checked at admission and at Pi's atomic commit boundary. Unlike the legacy optional spawn scope policy, this path resolves Pi patterns/globs against the full current registry, and malformed/unreadable settings, diagnostics and restricted-empty results refuse control. Project `enabledModels` overrides global; absent fields and explicit `[]` are unrestricted.
+
+Requires the additive public Pi conditional-configuration APIs and synchronous scope resolver; missing capability returns `unsupported`, without breaking ordinary Agent loading on Pi 0.84.2. Never waits for idle, resumes/aborts a child, changes global defaults, or falls back to raw setters. Identical operation retries retain stable validator/signal identity; conflicting reuse and new IDs beyond the 1024-per-record capacity are refused. Receipts are process-local. See [the exact types, refusal semantics and unit-test limits](docs/rpc.md#conditional-retained-idle-child-configuration).
+
